Step 1: Calculate Initial Cost

No moves have been made.

g(n) = 0

Using the Misplaced Tiles heuristic, tiles 5 and 8
are in the wrong positions.

h(n) = 2

Therefore:

f(n) = g(n) + h(n)
     = 0 + 2
     = 2

Step 2: Move Tile 5

Move tile 5 upward into the blank space.

+---+---+---+
| 1 | 2 | 3 |
+---+---+---+
| 4 | 5 | 6 |
+---+---+---+
| 7 |   | 8 |
+---+---+---+

Now:

g(n) = 1
h(n) = 1
f(n) = 1 + 1 = 2

Step 3: Move Tile 8

Move tile 8 to the left.

+---+---+---+
| 1 | 2 | 3 |
+---+---+---+
| 4 | 5 | 6 |
+---+---+---+
| 7 | 8 |   |
+---+---+---+

Now the goal state is reached.

g(n) = 2
h(n) = 0
f(n) = 2

Solution

The puzzle is solved in 2 moves.

Move 1: Tile 5 moves Up
Move 2: Tile 8 moves Left
